<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "The P2P Lobby is the persistent peer-to-peer connection behind /p2p: one link between two users that hosts a call, file transfers and games all at the same time. It lives inside the chat — accepting an invite opens the session windows right on the chat desktop, next to your conversations."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_p2p}>{dgettext("help_p2p", "One Connection, Every Feature")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "Once connected, the call starts automatically and the Files, Games and Statistics windows wait minimized on the taskbar. Everything runs concurrently over the same connection: send a file during the call, start a game without hanging up. Ending any one activity never drops the others — only ending the session does."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_p2p}>{dgettext("help_p2p", "Self-Controlled Media")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "Audio and video are self-controlled: each peer turns their own microphone and camera on or off independently, like a modern video call. File transfers and games still ask the other side to accept."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_p2p}>{dgettext("help_p2p", "Closing vs. Minimizing")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "Closing any session window disconnects the whole session (after a confirmation); minimizing keeps everything running in the taskbar. The status bar always shows the active session — click it to bring the windows back to the front."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_p2p", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="feature-p2p-in-chat">
    {dgettext("help_p2p", "P2P Sessions in Chat")}
  </.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-p2p">{dgettext("help_p2p", "/p2p")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="feature-video-call">{dgettext("help_p2p", "Video Call")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="feature-file-transfer">{dgettext("help_p2p", "File Transfer")}</.help_link>
</p>
